# Cursor + Grok Collaboration Rule

- Use one owner per task: either Cursor or Grok implements; the other reviews.
- Never edit the same file in parallel from both agents.
- Work in short-lived branches (`feat/*`, `fix/*`, `exp/grok-*`) and merge small PRs.
- Keep one source of truth for integration decisions before merge.

## Required outputs from Grok

- Proposed file list and scope boundaries.
- Risk/regression notes and rollback suggestion.
- Exact test commands to run.

## Merge safety checklist

- Confirm diff only touches expected files.
- Run lint/build/tests before opening or merging PR.
- Do not mix unrelated scopes in one PR.
- Keep feature flags default OFF for risky/operational changes.
